  "diagnostic_feedback": "The candidate constraint models a 'Not Co-Existence' between activities A_Denied and A_Pending, i.e., it forbids a loan denial and a pending disbursement from occurring together. The EU Directive 2008/48/EC Article 13(2) concerns the creditor's ability to terminate the consumer's right to draw down on an open‑end credit agreement and the mandatory information duties, not the outright denial of a loan application or the prohibition of subsequent disbursement. Consequently, the selected activities and the logical relation do not capture the termination‑and‑information requirements of the legal clause, nor do they reflect the informational timing obligations. The operational policy cited is also about post‑denial disbursement, which falls outside the scope of the cited directive. Therefore the AST does not faithfully implement the statutory provision."
}

